        return q('Bilinear-transform Butterworth design', T`Design a second-order digital Butterworth low-pass filter with $f_s = ${fs}\,\text{Hz}$ and $-3\,\text{dB}$ cutoff $f_c = ${fc}\,\text{Hz}$, using the bilinear transform $s = 2f_s\dfrac{1 - z^{-1}}{1 + z^{-1}}$ with prewarping. Write $$H(z) = b_0\,\frac{1 + 2z^{-1} + z^{-2}}{1 + a_1z^{-1} + a_2z^{-2}}.$$ Find the prewarped cutoff, the coefficients and the pole radius. Then find the gain at $2f_c$ (the analogue prototype gives $-12.3\,\text{dB}$) and the group delay at DC in samples.`, [T`$f_s = ${fs}\,\text{Hz}$`, T`$f_c = ${fc}\,\text{Hz}$`, 'Order 2, Butterworth', 'Bilinear with prewarping'], [p(T`$\Omega_c$`, Wc, 'rad/s'), p(T`$b_0$`, b0, ''), p(T`$a_1$`, a1, ''), p(T`$a_2$`, a2, ''), p('Pole radius', r, ''), p(T`Gain at $${2 * fc}\,\text{Hz}$`, hdb, 'dB'), p('Group delay at DC', gd, 'samples')], [T`Prewarp: $\Omega_c = 2f_s\tan(\pi f_c/f_s)$. Let $K = \tan(\pi f_c/f_s)$.`, T`Substitute into $\dfrac{\Omega_c^2}{s^2 + \sqrt2\Omega_cs + \Omega_c^2}$ and normalise by $1 + \sqrt2K + K^2$. The poles have radius $\sqrt{a_2}$.`, T`Evaluate $H(e^{j\omega})$ at $\omega = 2\pi\cdot2f_c/f_s$. Group delay is $-d\phi/d\omega$ at $\omega \to 0$.`], [T`$K = ${tf(K)}$ and $\Omega_c = ${tf(Wc)}\,\text{rad/s}$.`, T`$b_0 = \dfrac{K^2}{1 + \sqrt2K + K^2} = ${tf(b0)}$, $a_1 = ${tf(a1)}$, $a_2 = ${tf(a2)}$.`, T`Pole radius $\sqrt{a_2} = ${tf(r)}$ at angle $\pm${tf(deg(Math.acos(-a1 / (2 * r))))}^\circ$.`, T`$|H|$ at $${2 * fc}\,\text{Hz}$ $= ${tf(hdb)}\,\text{dB}$ versus $${tf(analog)}\,\text{dB}$ analogue: warping steepens the response towards Nyquist.`, T`Group delay at DC $= ${tf(gd)}$ samples $= ${tf(gd / fs * 1e6)}\,\mu\text{s}$.`], 'Prewarping pins one frequency exactly; everything else is warped by the tangent map.', hardBlock(`Digital Butterworth · fs = ${fs} Hz · fc = ${fc} Hz`, 'x[n] → b₀(1 + 2z⁻¹ + z⁻²) / (1 + a₁z⁻¹ + a₂z⁻²) → y[n]'), 'Bilinear transform; frequency warping; IIR filters; group delay.');
